## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
Severity: MEDIUM  
AMD operates in a cyclical semiconductor industry with high capital expenditure requirements. As a fab-lite company, it relies on foundries like TSMC, exposing it to supply chain risks. Additionally, customer concentration in the data center market (e.g., AI and cloud computing) creates revenue dependency, though diversification efforts mitigate this risk.  

